			"Message": "build(deps): bump pozil/auto-assign-issue from 2.2.0 to 3.0.0\n\nBumps [pozil/auto-assign-issue](https://github.com/pozil/auto-assign-issue) from 2.2.0 to 3.0.0.\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/pozil/auto-assign-issue/releases)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/pozil/auto-assign-issue/compare/v2.2.0...v3.0.0)\n\n---\nupdated-dependencies:\n- dependency-name: pozil/auto-assign-issue\n  dependency-version: 3.0.0\n  dependency-type: direct:production\n  update-type: version-update:semver-major\n...\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>",
			"SHA": "2076b7ee0358f662975968d821ccb2b50d179557"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-24T20:33:55Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				81,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Sky): Wire extension tree views into workbench rendering pipeline\n\nAdd native data provider attachment so extension-registered tree views actually render in the workbench pane. Stock VS Code uses ExtHostContext RPC to set `treeView.dataProvider` via `MainThreadTreeViews.$registerTreeViewDataProvider` - we don't have that channel yet (Track A bring-up), so Sky bridges it by:\n\n1. Exposing `TreeViewByViewId(id)` from the Output transform plugin - returns the same `ITreeView` the stock mainThread accesses via `Registry.as(ViewsRegistry).getView(id).treeView`\n\n2. Attaching a data provider in `cel:tree-view:create` that calls `tree:getChildren` via `MountainIPCInvoke`, converting Cocoon's wire shape (`{handle, label, isCollapsed, icon}`) into the workbench's `ITreeItem` shape (`handle, collapsibleState, label: {label}, ...`). Side-panel observers retain access to extended fields like `icon` that the renderer ignores.\n\n3. Retry logic (5 attempts, 150ms spacing) handles the case where the view is registered BEFORE the tree descriptor mounts - covers both async workbench init and collapsed-pane-not-yet-mounted.\n\n4. New `cel:tree-view:refresh` handler calls `treeView.refresh()` so extensions that fire `onDidChangeTreeData` update both the native pane and Sky observers.\n\n5. New `cel:tree-view:dispose` handler clears `dataProvider` so the workbench falls back to empty-state while keeping the pane registered.\n\nDual-emit persists: the DOM CustomEvent `cel:tree-view:items` stays for any Sky/Astro observer (side-panel mirror, diagnostic inspector) to react without going through the workbench pipeline.",
			"SHA": "3f5eee5f8571c9bb7a48ae27b4c1834c7b1ba66a"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-24T15:36:24Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				81,
				2
			],
			"Message": "feat(Sky): Add land-native search provider and global exception cap\n\nAdd a search result provider that routes VS Code's Search viewlet queries through Mountain's `search:findFiles` / `search:findInFiles` handlers. The stock web's `RemoteSearchService` relies on File System Access API which returns `undefined` for Land's Mountain-based filesystem, causing silent zero-result returns. The new provider registers for both `file` (0) and `text` (1) search types, translating Mountain hits into the `IFileMatch` shape the workbench expects.\n\nAlso add a global exception cap to PostHogBridge to prevent flooding posthog-js's CDN limit. The CDN enforces a hard 10 events/10s cap on `$exception` regardless of signature — a diverse-error boot could blow through this without a global counter. The cap is configurable via `LAND_POSTHOG_SKY_EXCEPTION_GLOBAL_LIMIT` (defaults to 7) and reports global drop metrics in the throttle summary.",
			"SHA": "b4358aa9cbb5b8231c3b6663778127863e708055"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-24T14:48:45Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				81,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Sky): Wire status bar and command bridges into workbench services\n\nReplaces the no-op status bar handlers from the previous commit with real integrations using the workbench services exposed via `__CEL_SERVICES__`. Extension-contributed status bar items from `vscode.window.createStatusBarItem(...)` now route through `IStatusbarService.addEntry()`, enabling them to render in the same `.statusbar` DOM as stock VS Code items.\n\nAdds a new command bridge layer that bridges Cocoon → workbench command invocations:\n- `sky://command/execute` calls `ICommandService.executeCommand` and resolves the result back to the extension\n- `sky://command/register` registers extension commands into `CommandsRegistry`, with invocation fan-out back to Cocoon via `ResolveUIRequest`\n- `sky://command/unregister` disposes the registration\n\nThe status bar set-message handler now only dispatches DOM CustomEvents for Sky-side observers rather than dual-routing, as the workbench handles ephemeral messages through its own path.\n\nThis completes the status bar integration that was previously deferred and enables extension commands to execute against the workbench.",
			"SHA": "ea2932ae02487b23967cbab690a7991ec1d19001"
		}
	],
